{"agent":"Monster3-fix-size-kill-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The added `(\"adapters/platform.py\", \"kill_group\")` entry contradicts the documented meaning of `OWN_CHILD_SITES`. The set is described as “a signal sent to a process that code started,” but the added comment says this function “delegates to `proc.kill_group`,” so it is not itself a signal-send site. If the test suppresses violations by file/function, this entry creates a hole: code such as `os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)` added inside `adapters/platform.py:kill_group` would be accepted because the function is whitelisted, even though `platform.kill_group` did not start `pid` and has no ownership proof there. The test’s promise that whitelisted sites only signal processes they launched is therefore not kept.","digest":"97ed8c17ba1d7a18","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_no_kill_paths.py:OWN_CHILD_SITES","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_no_kill_paths.py:OWN_CHILD_SITES"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":1280,"diff_sha":"ed77a586d393e3515b607e072f5bb3b10a06f2fd2752eb68014af182df8f277c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-size-kill","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":18.7,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"f64308685f704bdb","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-size-kill.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T140209Z-b8406ad1.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"79958a36344e","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-fix-size-kill-7267fe reviewed lane-drift-c's fix-size-kill","reviewed_head":"29bd1989a37b7fa9ab90b580956fc0247c812c0f","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_no_kill_paths.py":